      <fo:flow flow-name="xsl-region-body" start-indent="1in" end-indent="0pt">
         <fo:block id="service.tr069todmt">
            <fo:block font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
               <fo:block margin-left="0pt">
                  <fo:block font-size="24.8832pt" font-weight="bold">
                     <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                               xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                               keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                               space-before.optimum="0in"
                               space-before.minimum="0in"
                               space-before.maximum="0in"
                               hyphenate="false"
                               text-align="start"
                               start-indent="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                               font-size="28pt"
                               line-height="35pt"
                               font-weight="normal"
                               space-after="24pt">
                        <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                       provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                           <fo:list-item>
                              <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                 <fo:block>131</fo:block>
                              </fo:list-item-label>
                              <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                 <fo:block>TR069 Connector Service Specification</fo:block>
                              </fo:list-item-body>
                           </fo:list-item>
                        </fo:list-block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                               xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                               font-family="ProductusOSGiBookcItalic"
                               font-size="18pt"
                               line-height="25pt">
                        <fo:basic-link internal-destination="org.osgi.service.tr069todmt">
                           <fo:inline color="inherit"
                                      font-family="inherit"
                                      letter-spacing="inherit"
                                      hyphenate="inherit">Version 1.0</fo:inline>
                        </fo:basic-link>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block id="d207e87">
            <fo:block>
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                            margin-left="0pt"
                            font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                     <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                        <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                  xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                  font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                  font-weight="normal"
                                  keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                  space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                  space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                  space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                  text-align="start"
                                  start-indent="0pt"
                                  hyphenate="false">
                           <fo:marker marker-class-name="section.head.marker">Introduction</fo:marker>
                           <fo:block font-size="18pt"
                                     line-height="25pt"
                                     space-before="12.5pt"
                                     space-after="12pt">
                              <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                             provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                       <fo:block>131.1</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block>Introduction</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">This chapter provides a specification for the TR069 Connector, an
    assistant to a Protocol Adapter based on <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="i741499">
                  <fo:inline color="inherit"
                             font-family="inherit"
                             letter-spacing="inherit"
                             hyphenate="inherit">[1] <fo:inline font-style="italic">TR-069 Amendment 3</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link>. A
    TR069 Connector provides a mapping of TR-069 concepts to/from the <fo:inline color="inherit"
                          font-family="inherit"
                          letter-spacing="inherit"
                          hyphenate="inherit">???</fo:inline>. It mainly handles the low level details of
    Object/Parameter Name to Dmt Admin URI mapping, and vice versa. TR-069
    Protocol Adapter developers can use this service to simplify the use the
    Dmt Admin service. The TR069 Connector service is based on the definition
    of a Protocol Mapping in <fo:inline color="inherit"
                          font-family="inherit"
                          letter-spacing="inherit"
                          hyphenate="inherit">???</fo:inline>. It
    is assumed that the reader understands TR-069 and has a basic
    understanding of the Dmt Admin service.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">The examples in this specification are not from a Broadband Forum
    Technical Report and are purely fictional.</fo:block>
            <fo:block id="d207e98">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>131.1.1</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>Essentials</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:list-block space-before.optimum="1em"
                              space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                              space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                              space-after.optimum="1em"
                              space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                              space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                              provisional-label-separation="0.2em"
                              provisional-distance-between-starts="12pt"
                              id="d207e100">
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d207e101">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">Connector</fo:inline> - Provide a TR-069 view on top
          of the Dmt Admin service.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d207e105">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">Simplify</fo:inline> - Simplify the handling of data
          models implemented through the DMT through the TR-069
          protocol.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d207e109">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">Browse</fo:inline> - Implement the constructs for
          <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">MAP</fo:inline> and <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">LIST</fo:inline> handling.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d207e117">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">Native</fo:inline> - Provide a mechanism for Data
          Plugins to convey conversion information to the Protocol Adapter so
          that native TR-069 object models can be implemented as Data
          Plugins.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
               </fo:list-block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block id="d207e121">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>131.1.2</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>Entities</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:list-block space-before.optimum="1em"
                              space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                              space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                              space-after.optimum="1em"
                              space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                              space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                              provisional-label-separation="0.2em"
                              provisional-distance-between-starts="12pt"
                              id="d207e123">
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d207e124">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                             xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                             internal-destination="org.osgi.service.tr069todmt.TR069ConnectorFactory">
                                 <fo:inline color="blue"
                                            font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                            letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                            hyphenate="false">TR069ConnectorFactory</fo:inline>
                              </fo:basic-link> - Provides a way to create a <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                             xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                             internal-destination="org.osgi.service.tr069todmt.TR069Connector">
                                 <fo:inline color="blue"
                                            font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                            letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                            hyphenate="false">TR069Connector</fo:inline>
                              </fo:basic-link> that is bound to an active Dmt
          Session.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d207e130">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                             xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                             internal-destination="org.osgi.service.tr069todmt.TR069Connector">
                                 <fo:inline color="blue"
                                            font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                            letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                            hyphenate="false">TR069Connector</fo:inline>
                              </fo:basic-link> - Created by <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                             xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                             internal-destination="org.osgi.service.tr069todmt.TR069ConnectorFactory">
                                 <fo:inline color="blue"
                                            font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                            letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                            hyphenate="false">TR069ConnectorFactory</fo:inline>
                              </fo:basic-link> on a Dmt Session; provides methods that
          helps in using the TR-069 namespace and RPCs on a Dmt Admin
          DMT.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d207e136">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                             xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                             internal-destination="org.osgi.service.tr069todmt.ParameterValue">
                                 <fo:inline color="blue"
                                            font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                            letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                            hyphenate="false">ParameterValue</fo:inline>
                              </fo:basic-link> - The value of a parameter, maps to the
          TR-069 <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">ParameterValueStruct</fo:inline>.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d207e142">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                             xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                             internal-destination="org.osgi.service.tr069todmt.ParameterInfo">
                                 <fo:inline color="blue"
                                            font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                            letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                            hyphenate="false">ParameterInfo</fo:inline>
                              </fo:basic-link> - Information about the parameter, maps to
          the TR-069 <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">ParameterInfoStruct</fo:inline>.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d207e148">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>DMT - The Device Management Tree as available through the Dmt
          Admin service.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
               </fo:list-block>
               <fo:block space-before.minimum="0.5em"
                         space-before.optimum="1em"
                         space-before.maximum="2em"
                         space-after.minimum="0.5em"
                         space-after.optimum="1em"
                         space-after.maximum="2em"
                         keep-together.within-column="always"
                         id="i742559">
                  <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                            xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                            space-before.optimum="5pt"
                            space-before.minimum="5pt"
                            space-before.maximum="5pt"
                            font-weight="normal"
                            font-size="9pt"
                            hyphenate="false"
                            space-after.minimum="0.4em"
                            space-after.optimum="0.6em"
                            space-after.maximum="0.8em"
                            start-indent="0pt"
                            font-family="Proforma-Book,ArialUnicodeMS"
                            font-style="italic"
                            keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                     <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                    provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                        <fo:list-item>
                           <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                              <fo:block>Figure 131.1</fo:block>
                           </fo:list-item-label>
                           <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                              <fo:block>TR-069 Entities</fo:block>
                           </fo:list-item-body>
                        </fo:list-item>
                     </fo:list-block>
                  </fo:block>
                  <fo:block id="d207e152" text-align="center">
                     <fo:external-graphic src="url(file:///home/stbischof/git/OSGI_MIGRATE/osgi_target/org.osgi.service.tr069todmt/spec/org.osgi.spec.service.tr069todmt/src/main/resources/spec/tr069-classes.svg)"
                                          width="auto"
                                          height="auto"
                                          content-width="6.230in"
                                          content-height="1.501in"
                                          text-align="center"/>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block id="d207e155">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>131.1.3</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>Synopsis</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">A TR-069 Protocol Adapter first creates a Dmt Session on the node
      in the DMT that maps to an object model that should be visible to the
      TR-069 Management Server. A Protocol Adapter can choose to map a whole
      sub-tree or it can create a virtual object model based on different
      nodes, this depends on the implementation of the Protocol
      Adapter.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">When a TR-069 RPC arrives, the Protocol Adapter must parse the
      SOAP message and analyze the request. In general, an RPC can request the
      update or retrieval of multiple values. The Protocol Adapter must
      decompose these separate requests into single requests and execute them
      as a single unit. If the request is a retrieval or update of a data
      model maintained in the Dmt Admin service then the Protocol Adapter can
      use a TR069 Connector to simplify implementing this request. The TR069
      Connector Factory service can be used to create an instance of a TR069
      Connector that is based on a specific Dmt Session.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">The TR069 Connector maps the Object or Parameter Name to a URI and
      perform the requested operation on the corresponding node. The
      name-to-URI conversion supports the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">LIST</fo:inline> and
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">MAP</fo:inline> concepts as defined in <fo:inline color="inherit"
                             font-family="inherit"
                             letter-spacing="inherit"
                             hyphenate="inherit">???</fo:inline>.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">The TR069 Connector handles conversion from the Dmt Admin data
      types to the TR-069 data types. There is a default mapping for the
      standard Dmt Admin formats including the comma separated list supported
      by TR-069. However, Data Plugins that implement TR-069 aware object
      models can instruct the TR069 Connector by providing specific MIME types
      on the Meta Node.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">Objects can be added and deleted but are, in general, not added
      immediately. These objects are lazily created when they are accessed.
      The reason is that TR-069 does not support the concept of a session with
      atomic semantics, a fact leveraged by certain object models in the DMT.
      Therefore, adding an object will assign a instance id to an object but
      the creation of the object is delayed until the object is used.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">After all the requests in an RPC are properly handled the TR069
      Connector must be closed, the Dmt Session must be closed
      separately.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">Errors are reported to the caller as they happen, if a Dmt Admin
      service error is fatal then the Dmt Session will be closed and it will
      be necessary to create a new TR069 Connector.</fo:block>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block id="d207e171">
            <fo:block>
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                            margin-left="0pt"
                            font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                     <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                        <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                  xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                  font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                  font-weight="normal"
                                  keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                  space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                  space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                  space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                  text-align="start"
                                  start-indent="0pt"
                                  hyphenate="false">
                           <fo:marker marker-class-name="section.head.marker">TR-069 Protocol Primer</fo:marker>
                           <fo:block font-size="18pt"
                                     line-height="25pt"
                                     space-before="12.5pt"
                                     space-after="12pt">
                              <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                             provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                       <fo:block>131.2</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block>TR-069 Protocol Primer</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">The <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="i799974">
                  <fo:inline color="inherit"
                             font-family="inherit"
                             letter-spacing="inherit"
                             hyphenate="inherit">[6] <fo:inline font-style="italic">Broadband Forum</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> is an organization for broadband
    wire-line solutions. They develop multi-service broadband packet
    networking specifications addressing interoperability, architecture, and
    management. Their specifications enable home, business and converged
    broadband services, encompassing customer, access and backbone networks.
    One of the specifications of the Broadband Forum is the
    <fo:inline font-style="italic">Technical Report No 69</fo:inline>, also called TR-069, a
    specification of a management model.</fo:block>
            <fo:block id="d207e179">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>131.2.1</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>Architecture</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">
                  <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="i741499">
                     <fo:inline color="inherit"
                                font-family="inherit"
                                letter-spacing="inherit"
                                hyphenate="inherit">[1] <fo:inline font-style="italic">TR-069 Amendment 3</fo:inline>
                     </fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link> is a technical report (Broadband Forum's
      specification model) that specifies a management protocol based on <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="i741562">
                     <fo:inline color="inherit"
                                font-family="inherit"
                                letter-spacing="inherit"
                                hyphenate="inherit">[4] <fo:inline font-style="italic">SOAP 1.1</fo:inline>
                     </fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link> over HTTP. The TR-069 technical report defines a
      number of mandatory Remote Procedure Calls (RPCs) that allow a
      management system, the Auto-Configuration Server (ACS), to discover the
      capabilities of the Consumer Premises Equipment (CPE) and do basic
      management. This model is depicted in <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="i753210">
                     <fo:inline color="inherit"
                                font-family="inherit"
                                letter-spacing="inherit"
                                hyphenate="inherit">Figure 131.2</fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link>.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.minimum="0.5em"
                         space-before.optimum="1em"
                         space-before.maximum="2em"
                         space-after.minimum="0.5em"
                         space-after.optimum="1em"
                         space-after.maximum="2em"
                         keep-together.within-column="always"
                         id="i753210">
                  <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                            xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                            space-before.optimum="5pt"
                            space-before.minimum="5pt"
                            space-before.maximum="5pt"
                            font-weight="normal"
                            font-size="9pt"
                            hyphenate="false"
                            space-after.minimum="0.4em"
                            space-after.optimum="0.6em"
                            space-after.maximum="0.8em"
                            start-indent="0pt"
                            font-family="Proforma-Book,ArialUnicodeMS"
                            font-style="italic"
                            keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                     <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                    provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                        <fo:list-item>
                           <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                              <fo:block>Figure 131.2</fo:block>
                           </fo:list-item-label>
                           <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                              <fo:block>TR-069 Reference Architecture</fo:block>
                           </fo:list-item-body>
                        </fo:list-item>
                     </fo:list-block>
                  </fo:block>
                  <fo:block id="d207e190" text-align="center">
                     <fo:external-graphic src="url(file:///home/stbischof/git/OSGI_MIGRATE/osgi_target/org.osgi.service.tr069todmt/spec/org.osgi.spec.service.tr069todmt/src/main/resources/spec/ref-architecture.svg)"
                                          width="auto"
                                          height="auto"
                                          content-width="6.214in"
                                          content-height="0.750in"
                                          text-align="center"/>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">In TR-069, the CPE is always initiating the conversation with the
      ACS though the ACS can request a session.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">Inside the CPE there is a Protocol Adapter that implements the
      TR-069 RPCs. These RPCs read and modify the objects models present in
      the CPE. There is usually a mechanism that allows the different modules
      in the CPE to contribute a management object to the Protocol Adapter so
      that the Protocol Adapter does not require knowledge about highly
      specialized domains.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">
                  <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="i694602">
                     <fo:inline color="inherit"
                                font-family="inherit"
                                letter-spacing="inherit"
                                hyphenate="inherit">[2] <fo:inline font-style="italic">TR-106 Amendment 3</fo:inline>
                     </fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link> specifies object model guidelines to be
      followed by all TR-069-enabled devices as well as a formal model to
      document these object models.</fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block id="d207e198">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>131.2.2</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>Object Model</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">The object model of TR-069 consists of
      <fo:inline font-style="italic">objects</fo:inline> that contain
      <fo:inline font-style="italic">parameters</fo:inline> as well as <fo:inline font-style="italic">tables</fo:inline>
      that contain objects. TR-106 says:</fo:block>
               <fo:list-block space-before.optimum="1em"
                              space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                              space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                              space-after.optimum="1em"
                              space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                              space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                              provisional-label-separation="0.2em"
                              provisional-distance-between-starts="12pt"
                              id="d207e208">
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d207e209">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">Object</fo:inline> - A named collection of parameters
          and/or other objects.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d207e213">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">Parameter</fo:inline> - A name-value pair.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d207e217">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">Table</fo:inline> - An enumeration of objects
          identified by an instance id.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
               </fo:list-block>
               <fo:block start-indent="0pt">
                  <fo:block space-before.minimum="0.5em"
                            space-before.optimum="1em"
                            space-before.maximum="2em"
                            space-after.minimum="0.5em"
                            space-after.optimum="1em"
                            space-after.maximum="2em"
                            keep-together.within-column="always"
                            id="d207e221">
                     <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                               xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                               space-before.optimum="5pt"
                               space-before.minimum="5pt"
                               space-before.maximum="5pt"
                               font-weight="normal"
                               font-size="9pt"
                               hyphenate="false"
                               space-after.minimum="0.4em"
                               space-after.optimum="0.6em"
                               space-after.maximum="0.8em"
                               start-indent="0pt"
                               font-family="Proforma-Book,ArialUnicodeMS"
                               font-style="italic"
                               keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                        <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                       provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                           <fo:list-item>
                              <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                 <fo:block>Figure 131.3</fo:block>
                              </fo:list-item-label>
                              <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                 <fo:block>Type Model TR-069</fo:block>
                              </fo:list-item-body>
                           </fo:list-item>
                        </fo:list-block>
                     </fo:block>
                     <fo:block id="d207e223" text-align="center">
                        <fo:external-graphic src="url(file:///home/stbischof/git/OSGI_MIGRATE/osgi_target/org.osgi.service.tr069todmt/spec/org.osgi.spec.service.tr069todmt/src/main/resources/spec/type-model.svg)"
                                             width="auto"
                                             height="auto"
                                             content-width="6.259in"
                                             content-height="1.874in"
                                             text-align="center"/>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">Objects can also occur in tables, in that case the object name is
      suffixed with an <fo:inline font-style="italic">instance id</fo:inline>. An object that has no
      instance id is a singleton, with an instance id they are referred to as
      <fo:inline font-style="italic">tables</fo:inline>. In the Broadband Forum technical reports
      tables end in the special suffix <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">{i}</fo:inline>, the instance
      id.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">This provides the following structural definition for this
      specification:</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                         space-before.optimum="1em"
                         space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                         space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                         space-after.optimum="1em"
                         space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                         hyphenate="false"
                         wrap-option="no-wrap"
                         white-space-collapse="false"
                         white-space-treatment="preserve"
                         linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                         text-align="start"
                         font-family="ProductusOSGiMonoc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                         font-size="9pt"
                         letter-spacing="-.0em"
                         space-before="5pt"
                         space-after="3pt"
                         space-after.conditionality="retain"
                         start-indent="inherit"
                         line-height="11pt"
                         id="d207e235">named-value ::= NAME ( object | table | parameter )
object      ::= named-value +
table       ::= ( instance object )*
parameter   ::=
instance    ::= INTEGER &gt; 0</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">TR-069 talks about partial paths and parameter names. In this
      specification, a <fo:inline font-style="italic">name</fo:inline> is reserved for the short
      relative name used inside an object, also called the <fo:inline font-style="italic">local
      name</fo:inline>. The term <fo:inline font-style="italic">path</fo:inline> is reserved for the
      combination of object names, table names, and instance ids that are
      separated by a full stop (<fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">'.' \u002E</fo:inline>) and used to traverse
      an instance model.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                         space-before.optimum="1em"
                         space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                         space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                         space-after.optimum="1em"
                         space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                         hyphenate="false"
                         wrap-option="no-wrap"
                         white-space-collapse="false"
                         white-space-treatment="preserve"
                         linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                         text-align="start"
                         font-family="ProductusOSGiMonoc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                         font-size="9pt"
                         letter-spacing="-.0em"
                         space-before="5pt"
                         space-after="3pt"
                         space-after.conditionality="retain"
                         start-indent="inherit"
                         line-height="11pt"
                         id="d207e246">path           ::= parameter-path | object-path| table-path
segment        ::= NAME '.' ( instance '.' )?
object-path    ::= segment+
table-path     ::= segment* NAME '.'   // expect INTEGER next
parameter-path ::= object-path NAME
instance-path  ::= table-path instance '.'</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">In this specification the following terms are used
      consistently:</fo:block>
               <fo:list-block space-before.optimum="1em"
                              space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                              space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                              space-after.optimum="1em"
                              space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                              space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                              provisional-label-separation="0.2em"
                              provisional-distance-between-starts="12pt"
                              id="d207e248">
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d207e249">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">Object</fo:inline> - Refers to a named type defining
          a certain set of parameters, objects, and tables.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d207e253">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">Table</fo:inline> - A list of instances for a given
          object.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d207e257">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">Instance</fo:inline> - An object element in a table
          at a certain id.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d207e261">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">Instance Id</fo:inline> - The integer id used to
          identify an instance in a table.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d207e265">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">Alias</fo:inline> - A name chosen by the ACS that
          uniquely identifies an instance.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d207e269">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">Singleton</fo:inline> - An object that is not in a
          table.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d207e273">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">Name</fo:inline> - The name of an object, table, or
          parameter refers to the local name only and not the path.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d207e277">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">Segment</fo:inline> - A component in a path that
          always ends in a full stop. A segment can contain instance ids to
          identify an instance.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d207e281">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">Path</fo:inline> - A string uniquely identifying a
          path in the tree to either a parameter, an object, or a
          table.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d207e285">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">Object Path</fo:inline> - A path that uniquely
          identifies an instance or a singleton. An object path must always
          ends in a full stop. This maps to the TR-069 concept of an
          <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">ObjectName</fo:inline>.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d207e291">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">Parameter Path</fo:inline> - The name of the
          parameter preceded by the owning object. A path that does not end in
          a full stop is always a parameter path.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d207e296">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">Table Path</fo:inline> - An object path that lacks
          the last instance id. In TR-069 this is also sometimes called a
          partial path. The last segment is an object path that must be
          followed by an instance id to address an instance.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d207e300">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">Instance Path</fo:inline> - A path to an instance in
          a table</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
               </fo:list-block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">This provides a hierarchy as depicted in <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="i808992">
                     <fo:inline color="inherit"
                                font-family="inherit"
                                letter-spacing="inherit"
                                hyphenate="inherit">Figure 131.4</fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link>.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.minimum="0.5em"
                         space-before.optimum="1em"
                         space-before.maximum="2em"
                         space-after.minimum="0.5em"
                         space-after.optimum="1em"
                         space-after.maximum="2em"
                         keep-together.within-column="always"
                         id="i808992">
                  <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                            xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                            space-before.optimum="5pt"
                            space-before.minimum="5pt"
                            space-before.maximum="5pt"
                            font-weight="normal"
                            font-size="9pt"
                            hyphenate="false"
                            space-after.minimum="0.4em"
                            space-after.optimum="0.6em"
                            space-after.maximum="0.8em"
                            start-indent="0pt"
                            font-family="Proforma-Book,ArialUnicodeMS"
                            font-style="italic"
                            keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                     <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                    provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                        <fo:list-item>
                           <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                              <fo:block>Figure 131.4</fo:block>
                           </fo:list-item-label>
                           <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                              <fo:block>TR-069 Object and Parameter naming relative to the parameter
        MemoryStatus</fo:block>
                           </fo:list-item-body>
                        </fo:list-item>
                     </fo:list-block>
                  </fo:block>
                  <fo:block id="d207e311" text-align="center">
                     <fo:external-graphic src="url(file:///home/stbischof/git/OSGI_MIGRATE/osgi_target/org.osgi.service.tr069todmt/spec/org.osgi.spec.service.tr069todmt/src/main/resources/spec/naming.svg)"
                                          width="auto"
                                          height="auto"
                                          content-width="5.011in"
                                          content-height="1.913in"
                                          text-align="center"/>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block id="i760050">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>131.2.3</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>Parameter Names</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">The grammars for parameter names and object names are as
      follows:</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                         space-before.optimum="1em"
                         space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                         space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                         space-after.optimum="1em"
                         space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                         hyphenate="false"
                         wrap-option="no-wrap"
                         white-space-collapse="false"
                         white-space-treatment="preserve"
                         linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                         text-align="start"
                         font-family="ProductusOSGiMonoc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                         font-size="9pt"
                         letter-spacing="-.0em"
                         space-before="5pt"
                         space-after="3pt"
                         space-after.conditionality="retain"
                         start-indent="inherit"
                         line-height="11pt"
                         id="d207e317">NAME ::= ( Letter | '_' )
         ( Letter | Digit | '-' | '_' | CombiningChar| Extender )*</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">The productions <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Letter</fo:inline>, <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Digit</fo:inline>,
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">CombiningChar</fo:inline>, and <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Extender</fo:inline> are defined in
      <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="i747814">
                     <fo:inline color="inherit"
                                font-family="inherit"
                                letter-spacing="inherit"
                                hyphenate="inherit">[5] <fo:inline font-style="italic">Extensible Markup Language (XML) 1.0 (Second Edition)</fo:inline>
                     </fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link>. The name basically supports the full Unicode
      character set for letters and digits (including digits for other
      languages), including sets for languages like Hebrew and Chinese.
      Examples of different parameter names are:</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                         space-before.optimum="1em"
                         space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                         space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                         space-after.optimum="1em"
                         space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                         hyphenate="false"
                         wrap-option="no-wrap"
                         white-space-collapse="false"
                         white-space-treatment="preserve"
                         linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                         text-align="start"
                         font-family="ProductusOSGiMonoc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                         font-size="9pt"
                         letter-spacing="-.0em"
                         space-before="5pt"
                         space-after="3pt"
                         space-after.conditionality="retain"
                         start-indent="inherit"
                         line-height="11pt"
                         id="d207e330">name            // simple name
Name            // case sensitive
_                           
_-_-_
ångstrom            
þingsten
<fo:inline xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                             xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                             font-family="ArialUnicodeMS">ΨΣΩΠ</fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block id="i786112">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>131.2.4</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>Parameter Type</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">A parameter value can have one of the data types defined in <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="i694602">
                     <fo:inline color="inherit"
                                font-family="inherit"
                                letter-spacing="inherit"
                                hyphenate="inherit">[2] <fo:inline font-style="italic">TR-106 Amendment 3</fo:inline>
                     </fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link>, they are summarized in <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="service.tr069todmt-tr106.data.types">
                     <fo:inline color="inherit"
                                font-family="inherit"
                                letter-spacing="inherit"
                                hyphenate="inherit">Table 131.1</fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link>.</fo:block>
               <fo:block xmlns:rx="http://www.renderx.com/XSL/Extensions"
                         space-before.minimum="0.5em"
                         space-before.optimum="1em"
                         space-before.maximum="2em"
                         space-after.minimum="0.5em"
                         space-after.optimum="1em"
                         space-after.maximum="2em"
                         keep-together.within-column="auto"
                         id="service.tr069todmt-tr106.data.types">
                  <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                            xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                            space-before.optimum="5pt"
                            space-before.minimum="5pt"
                            space-before.maximum="5pt"
                            font-weight="normal"
                            font-size="9pt"
                            hyphenate="false"
                            space-after.minimum="0.4em"
                            space-after.optimum="0.6em"
                            space-after.maximum="0.8em"
                            start-indent="0pt"
                            font-family="Proforma-Book,ArialUnicodeMS"
                            font-style="italic"
                            keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                     <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                    provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                        <fo:list-item>
                           <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                              <fo:block>Table 131.1</fo:block>
                           </fo:list-item-label>
                           <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                              <fo:block>TR-106 Data types</fo:block>
                           </fo:list-item-body>
                        </fo:list-item>
                     </fo:list-block>
                  </fo:block>
                  <fo:table border-before-width.conditionality="retain"
                            border-collapse="collapse"
                            table-layout="fixed"
                            width="100%">
                     <fo:table-column column-number="1" column-width="proportional-column-width(1)"/>
                     <fo:table-column column-number="2" column-width="proportional-column-width(3)"/>
                     <fo:table-header start-indent="0pt" end-indent="0pt">
                        <fo:table-row keep-together.within-column="always"
                                      keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                      font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                           <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                          padding-end="4pt"
                                          padding-top="1pt"
                                          padding-bottom="1pt">
                              <fo:block>TR-106 Type</fo:block>
                           </fo:table-cell>
                           <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                          padding-end="4pt"
                                          padding-top="1pt"
                                          padding-bottom="1pt">
                              <fo:block>Description</fo:block>
                           </fo:table-cell>
                        </fo:table-row>
                     </fo:table-header>
                     <fo:table-body start-indent="0pt" end-indent="0pt">
                        <fo:table-row keep-together.within-column="always">
                           <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                          padding-end="4pt"
                                          padding-top="1pt"
                                          padding-bottom="1pt">
                              <fo:block>
                                 <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                            font-size="9pt"
                                            letter-spacing="0.08em">object</fo:inline>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:table-cell>
                           <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                          padding-end="4pt"
                                          padding-top="1pt"
                                          padding-bottom="1pt">
                              <fo:block>
                                 <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                                           space-before.minimum="5pt"
                                           space-before.maximum="5pt">Represents a structured type</fo:block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:table-cell>
                        </fo:table-row>
                        <fo:table-row keep-together.within-column="always">
                           <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                          padding-end="4pt"
                                          padding-top="1pt"
                                          padding-bottom="1pt">
                              <fo:block>
                                 <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                            font-size="9pt"
                                            letter-spacing="0.08em">string</fo:inline>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:table-cell>
                           <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                          padding-end="4pt"
                                          padding-top="1pt"
                                          padding-bottom="1pt">
                              <fo:block>
                                 <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                                           space-before.minimum="5pt"
                                           space-before.maximum="5pt">A Unicode string, optionally restricted in
              length</fo:block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:table-cell>
                        </fo:table-row>
                        <fo:table-row keep-together.within-column="always">
                           <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                          padding-end="4pt"
                                          padding-top="1pt"
                                          padding-bottom="1pt">
                              <fo:block>
                                 <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                            font-size="9pt"
                                            letter-spacing="0.08em">int</fo:inline>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:table-cell>
                           <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                          padding-end="4pt"
                                          padding-top="1pt"
                                          padding-bottom="1pt">
                              <fo:block>
                                 <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                                           space-before.minimum="5pt"
                                           space-before.maximum="5pt">32 bit integer</fo:block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:table-cell>
                        </fo:table-row>
                        <fo:table-row keep-together.within-column="always">
                           <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                          padding-end="4pt"
                                          padding-top="1pt"
                                          padding-bottom="1pt">
                              <fo:block>
                                 <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                            font-size="9pt"
                                            letter-spacing="0.08em">long</fo:inline>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:table-cell>
                           <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                          padding-end="4pt"
                                          padding-top="1pt"
                                          padding-bottom="1pt">
                              <fo:block>
                                 <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                                           space-before.minimum="5pt"
                                           space-before.maximum="5pt">64 bit integer</fo:block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:table-cell>
                        </fo:table-row>
                        <fo:table-row keep-together.within-column="always">
                           <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                          padding-end="4pt"
                                          padding-top="1pt"
                                          padding-bottom="1pt">
                              <fo:block>
                                 <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                            font-size="9pt"
                                            letter-spacing="0.08em">unsignedInt</fo:inline>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:table-cell>
                           <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                          padding-end="4pt"
                                          padding-top="1pt"
                                          padding-bottom="1pt">
                              <fo:block>
                                 <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                                           space-before.minimum="5pt"
                                           space-before.maximum="5pt">32 bit unsigned integer</fo:block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:table-cell>
                        </fo:table-row>
                        <fo:table-row keep-together.within-column="always">
                           <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                          padding-end="4pt"
                                          padding-top="1pt"
                                          padding-bottom="1pt">
                              <fo:block>
                                 <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                            font-size="9pt"
                                            letter-spacing="0.08em">unsignedLong</fo:inline>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:table-cell>
                           <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                          padding-end="4pt"
                                          padding-top="1pt"
                                          padding-bottom="1pt">
                              <fo:block>
                                 <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                                           space-before.minimum="5pt"
                                           space-before.maximum="5pt">64 bit unsigned integer</fo:block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:table-cell>
                        </fo:table-row>
                        <fo:table-row keep-together.within-column="always">
                           <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                          padding-end="4pt"
                                          padding-top="1pt"
                                          padding-bottom="1pt">
                              <fo:block>
                                 <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                            font-size="9pt"
                                            letter-spacing="0.08em">boolean</fo:inline>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:table-cell>
                           <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                          padding-end="4pt"
                                          padding-top="1pt"
                                          padding-bottom="1pt">
                              <fo:block>
                                 <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                                           space-before.minimum="5pt"
                                           space-before.maximum="5pt">Can have values 0 or false (<fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                               font-size="9pt"
                                               letter-spacing="0.08em">false</fo:inline>) or
              1 or true (<fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                               font-size="9pt"
                                               letter-spacing="0.08em">true</fo:inline>)</fo:block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:table-cell>
                        </fo:table-row>
                        <fo:table-row keep-together.within-column="always">
                           <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                          padding-end="4pt"
                                          padding-top="1pt"
                                          padding-bottom="1pt">
                              <fo:block>
                                 <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                            font-size="9pt"
                                            letter-spacing="0.08em">dateTime</fo:inline>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:table-cell>
                           <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                          padding-end="4pt"
                                          padding-top="1pt"
                                          padding-bottom="1pt">
                              <fo:block>
                                 <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                                           space-before.minimum="5pt"
                                           space-before.maximum="5pt">TR-069 recognizes three different date times. These
              three cases are differentiated in the following
              way:</fo:block>
                                 <fo:list-block space-before.optimum="1em"
                                                space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                                space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                                space-after.optimum="1em"
                                                space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                                                space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.2em"
                                                provisional-distance-between-starts="12pt"
                                                id="d207e397">
                                    <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                                  space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                                  space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                                  id="d207e398">
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                                          <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>
                                             <fo:block>
                                                <fo:inline font-style="italic">Unknown time</fo:inline> - If the time is
                    not known.</fo:block>
                                          </fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                                  space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                                  space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                                  id="d207e402">
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                                          <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>
                                             <fo:block>
                                                <fo:inline font-style="italic">Relative time</fo:inline> - Relative time
                    is the time since boot time.</fo:block>
                                          </fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                                  space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                                  space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                                  id="d207e406">
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                                          <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>
                                             <fo:block>
                                                <fo:inline font-style="italic">Absolute time</fo:inline> - Normal date and
                    time.</fo:block>
                                          </fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:table-cell>
                        </fo:table-row>
                        <fo:table-row keep-together.within-column="always">
                           <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                          padding-end="4pt"
                                          padding-top="1pt"
                                          padding-bottom="1pt">
                              <fo:block>
                                 <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                            font-size="9pt"
                                            letter-spacing="0.08em">base64</fo:inline>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:table-cell>
                           <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                          padding-end="4pt"
                                          padding-top="1pt"
                                          padding-bottom="1pt">
                              <fo:block>
                                 <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                                           space-before.minimum="5pt"
                                           space-before.maximum="5pt">An array of bytes</fo:block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:table-cell>
                        </fo:table-row>
                        <fo:table-row keep-together.within-column="always">
                           <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                          padding-end="4pt"
                                          padding-top="1pt"
                                          padding-bottom="1pt">
                              <fo:block>
                                 <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                            font-size="9pt"
                                            letter-spacing="0.08em">hexBinary</fo:inline>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:table-cell>
                           <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                          padding-end="4pt"
                                          padding-top="1pt"
                                          padding-bottom="1pt">
                              <fo:block>
                                 <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                                           space-before.minimum="5pt"
                                           space-before.maximum="5pt">An array of bytes</fo:block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:table-cell>
                        </fo:table-row>
                     </fo:table-body>
                  </fo:table>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">SOAP messages always provide a type for the parameter value. For
      example:</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                         space-before.optimum="1em"
                         space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                         space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                         space-after.optimum="1em"
                         space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                         hyphenate="false"
                         wrap-option="no-wrap"
                         white-space-collapse="false"
                         white-space-treatment="preserve"
                         linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                         text-align="start"
                         font-family="ProductusOSGiMonoc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                         font-size="9pt"
                         letter-spacing="-.0em"
                         space-before="5pt"
                         space-after="3pt"
                         space-after.conditionality="retain"
                         start-indent="inherit"
                         line-height="11pt"
                         id="d207e421">&lt;ParameterValueStruct&gt;
  &lt;name&gt;Parameter1&lt;/name&gt;
  &lt;value xsi:type="long"&gt;1234&lt;/value&gt;
&lt;/ParameterValueStruct&gt;</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">The <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">xsi</fo:inline> prefix refers to the
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">https://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance</fo:inline> namespace.
      However, this makes not all TR-106 types well defined, for example in
      XML Schema <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">base64</fo:inline> is called <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">base64Binary</fo:inline>. This
      specification assumes that the names and definitions in <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="service.tr069todmt-tr106.data.types">
                     <fo:inline color="inherit"
                                font-family="inherit"
                                letter-spacing="inherit"
                                hyphenate="inherit">Table 131.1</fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link> and provides appropriate
      constants for the Protocol Adapter.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">Parameters can be read-only or read-write. All writable Parameters
      must also be readable although security can cause certain parameters to
      be read as an empty string, for example passwords. Parameters can
      reflect configuration as well as status of the device. External causes
      can cause parameters to change at any time. The TR-069 protocol has the
      facility to call an <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Inform</fo:inline> RPC to provide the ACS with a
      notification of changed parameters.</fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block id="d207e438">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>131.2.5</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>Parameter Attributes</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">Parameter attributes provide the meta data for a parameter. In
      TR-069, the attributes are used to manage notifications and access
      control. Each parameter in TR-069 can be watched by the ACS by setting
      the corresponding parameter attribute to <fo:inline font-style="italic">active</fo:inline> or
      <fo:inline font-style="italic">passive notifications</fo:inline>. Passive notifications are
      passed whenever the CPE communicates with the ACS and active
      notifications initiate a session. Parameters that have a notification
      are said to be <fo:inline font-style="italic">watched</fo:inline>.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">Access to the parameters can be managed by setting Access Control
      Lists via the corresponding parameter attribute.</fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block id="i831294">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>131.2.6</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>Objects and Tables</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">TR-106 has the concept of an <fo:inline font-style="italic">object</fo:inline> stored in
      a <fo:inline font-style="italic">table</fo:inline> to allow multiple instances of the same
      type. It is part of the object definition if it is stored in a table or
      not. An object cannot both appear as a table instance and as a
      singleton.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">Each instance in the table is addressed with an integer &gt;= 1.
      This <fo:inline font-style="italic">instance id</fo:inline> is not chosen by the ACS since it
      can be required to create a new instance due to an external event. For
      example the user plugging in a USB device or starting a new VOIP
      session. The ACS must discover these instance ids by asking the device
      for the instance ids in a table.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">For example, the parameter path
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Device.LAN.DHCPOption.4.Request</fo:inline> refers to a parameter on a
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">DHCPOption</fo:inline> object that has the instance id 4. Instance ids
      are not sequential nor predictable. It is the responsibility of the
      device to choose an instance id when an object is created. Instance ids
      are assumed to be persistent so that the ACS can cache results from a
      discovery process.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">Newer TR-069 objects have been given an <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Alias</fo:inline>
      parameter. This alias uniquely identifies the table instance.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">TR-069 defines a convention for a parameter that contains the
      number of entries in a table. Any parameter name that ends with
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">NumberOfEntries</fo:inline> contains the number of entries in a table
      with the name of the prefix in the same object. For example
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">A.B.CNumberOfEntries</fo:inline> provides the number of entries in the
      table:</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                         space-before.optimum="1em"
                         space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                         space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                         space-after.optimum="1em"
                         space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                         hyphenate="false"
                         wrap-option="no-wrap"
                         white-space-collapse="false"
                         white-space-treatment="preserve"
                         linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                         text-align="start"
                         font-family="ProductusOSGiMonoc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                         font-size="9pt"
                         letter-spacing="-.0em"
                         space-before="5pt"
                         space-after="3pt"
                         space-after.conditionality="retain"
                         start-indent="inherit"
                         line-height="11pt"
                         id="d207e477">A.B.C.</fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block id="d207e478">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>131.2.7</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>RPCs</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">The object model implemented in a device is accessed and modified
      with <fo:inline font-style="italic">RPCs</fo:inline>. RPCs are remote procedure calls; a way
      to invoke a function remotely. TR-069 defines a number of mandatory RPCs
      and provides a mechanism to extend and discover the set of RPCs
      implemented by a CPE. The mandatory RPCs are listed in in the following
      table.</fo:block>
               <fo:block xmlns:rx="http://www.renderx.com/XSL/Extensions"
                         space-before.minimum="0.5em"
                         space-before.optimum="1em"
                         space-before.maximum="2em"
                         space-after.minimum="0.5em"
                         space-after.optimum="1em"
                         space-after.maximum="2em"
                         keep-together.within-column="auto"
                         id="d207e484">
                  <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                            xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                            space-before.optimum="5pt"
                            space-before.minimum="5pt"
                            space-before.maximum="5pt"
                            font-weight="normal"
                            font-size="9pt"
                            hyphenate="false"
