               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">If the conversion fails and there are untried formats left then
      the other formats must be used.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">There is a special case when the destination node is a LIST node
      with primitive children and the source is a <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">string</fo:inline> type. In
      that case the string must be parsed according to TR-106 comma separated
      lists and each element must be stored as a child node.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">The conversion matrix is in the following table. The equal sign
      indicates identity taking into account any encoding. It is not necessary
      that the source type corresponds to a MIME type in the meta node.</fo:block>
